## Three roots, never mixed

| Purpose | Path |
|---|---|
| Code and configuration (git) | `<code root, for example C:\dev\research\>` |
| Data, outputs, figures, presentations | `<data root, for example C:\Users\you\OneDrive - Your University\research\>` |
| Knowledge (notes vault) | `<vault, for example C:\Users\you\OneDrive - Your University\Vault\>` |

Code never goes to the data root and data never into git, because git cannot forget a file once it
is pushed, and a synchronised drive and git fight over the same files. Write notes in the vault
<through the notes connector when the session has it, because the editor rewrites an open note>.

**Never search a cloud-synchronised root recursively** (`find`, `grep -r`, a glob from the root):
every file a search touches is downloaded in full. Go to the known path, or list one folder.

The guard hook enforces the originals and the write scope; this file only says why.

