## Maintaining this file

When I state a preference or a rule about future behaviour, the `learn` skill decides where it
goes: a hook if it is mechanical, the skill that owns the workflow if it has a trigger, this file
only if it fires on ordinary output, memory if it is a preference or project state. Every change
gets a dated line in `.claude/rules-changelog.md`, so the reason survives without costing a line
here. Past 200 lines, something moves out before anything comes in.
